---
title: Interaction
description: This system has two signature interactions, and they are built into the components rather than added by hand. Everything else is deliberately left out. A site that answers every touch with a different flourish feels busy; one that answers the same way every time feels designed.
eyebrow: Motion
source: src/components/button.css · card.css · src/motion/micro.css
---
<h2>One · the button leans</h2>
<p>A button gives under the press, and a <strong>trailing</strong> icon leans the way the button is going. Nothing else moves. It is automatic — there is no class to add.</p>
{{#example center=true}}
<a class="im-btn im-btn-primary im-btn-lg" href="#one-the-button-leans">Get started {{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</a>
<a class="im-btn" href="#one-the-button-leans">Read the docs {{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</a>
<a class="im-btn im-btn-outline" href="#one-the-button-leans">Open {{> "icons/arrow-up-right"}}</a>
<a class="im-btn im-btn-ghost" href="#one-the-button-leans">{{> "icons/download"}} A leading icon stays still</a>
{{/example}}
<p>Only an icon that comes <em>after</em> the label leans: that is the one that says "this goes somewhere". A leading icon names the action and stays put.</p>

<h2>Two · the edge sharpens</h2>
<p>A card is a ruled box, and it answers by <strong>drawing its rule</strong>: the hairline turns to ink, and its CTA arrow leans — the same lean as the button. No lift, no shadow, no tilt. Also automatic, for any card that is a link or holds a title link.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 14rem">
	<a class="im-card im-card-outline im-card-link" href="#two-the-edge-sharpens"><span class="im-card-title">An outlined card</span><span>Hover me: hairline → ink.</span><span class="im-card-cta">Read {{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</span></a>
	<article class="im-card im-card-outline"><div class="im-card-media"><img src="{{demo.post.feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></div><div class="im-card-body"><h3 class="im-card-title"><a href="#two-the-edge-sharpens">A card with media</a></h3><span class="im-card-cta">Read {{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</span></div></article>
	<a class="im-card im-card-link" href="#two-the-edge-sharpens"><span class="im-card-title">A filled card</span><span>Has no edge to sharpen, so it steps up one surface shade instead.</span></a>
</div>
{{/example}}
<p>The same gesture runs through the system: the <a href="/navigation/pagination/#previous-next-article">post nav</a> arrows lean, the <a href="/effects/border/#corners">corner brackets</a> run along their edges, an <a href="/forms/inputs/#states">input</a>'s hairline becomes a 2px rule on focus. One idea, repeated, is what makes a site feel like one thing.</p>

