<h2>What was left out, on purpose</h2>
<p>Earlier versions had ripple, magnetic buttons, 3D tilt, a pointer spotlight, swapping labels and spinning icons. Each is fine alone; together they are a toy box, and none of them belongs to a ruled, typographic system. They were removed. If a project truly needs one, it is twenty lines — but ask first whether the two above already say it.</p>
<ul>
	<li><strong>Answer within 100ms.</strong> A press must respond at once, even if the work takes longer.</li>
	<li><strong>One interaction per element.</strong></li>
	<li><strong>Hover is a bonus, never the only way.</strong> Everything here also fires on keyboard focus, and none of it carries information a touch user would miss.</li>
</ul>
